<!--
  THE ONE HEADER EVERY EXOCORTEX SCREEN ON main-page USES.

    Exocortex — <the app open on the glasses> — <connection>  [⚠] [⚙]

  Chris, using the real build (2026-08-31), gave this a number: 80-85% of the
  companion screen should be the app's own content. What he was actually
  looking at was five stacked bands of chrome before a single line of session
  showed —

    1  faceclaw's ActionBar          "Faceclaw            Connected"
    2  the app-switch bar            "Ghost is open on the glasses   [Hub]"
    3  the companion's wordmark row  "GHOST      Rich view"
    4  the companion's status row    "20 in the feed - session ghost-..."
    5  the pane tab bar              [Terminal][Rich][Doc][Settings]

  Bands 2, 3 and 4 collapsed into this single row, and band 1 was hidden while
  a companion showed. ROUND 3 finished that: main-page has no ActionBar at all
  now, so this row is the whole of its chrome, on the home body as well as on a
  companion — which is why the two right-hand segments exist. Both were the
  ActionBar's, and neither costs a pixel of height in a row that was already
  drawn.

    ⚠  the warning triangle, collapsed unless there is an actual warning.
       Opens the same "Attention needed" modal, which still lives in
       main-page.xml. It is now visible on the companion too, where the
       hidden ActionBar had taken it away.
    ⚙  Settings — phone-ui/settings-hub-page, which is faceclaw's old hub and
       carries the whole overflow menu the ActionBar used to. This is the one
       new affordance round 3 needed: with the bar gone there was no route off
       the home body, and a "Settings" ROW in the app list would have collided
       with the glasses' own Settings app, which is a row in that same list.

  DELIBERATELY NOT GHOST-SPECIFIC. Nothing here names Ghost: the app segment
  is whatever the glasses report as foreground. This is the chrome half of the
  generalized per-app companion mechanism that is still queued as its own
  design job — that one decides WHICH view shows per app, this one is the
  frame all of those views sit in. A new per-app companion added later inherits
  this header by being dropped into main-page.xml's companion body; it does not
  have to build, or re-litigate, a header of its own.

  Binds to MainViewModel, inherited from the page — NOT to the per-app view
  model underneath it. Everything in this row is about the app/phone/glasses
  relationship, which no single app's companion owns.

  "Exocortex" is the tap target back to the home body — the app list. From a
  companion it is the way out; on the home body it is already where you are,
  and tapping it is a no-op that re-asserts the same state.

  NOT ON THE COVER GLANCE, deliberately: that screen is one screenful by
  design and already carries the connection and the foreground app itself.
  The cost, stated rather than buried: with main-page's ActionBar gone, the
  warning triangle is not reachable while the Fold is shut. Unfolding is one
  motion, and every action behind that modal wants the inner screen anyway.
-->
<GridLayout xmlns="http://schemas.nativescript.org/tns.xsd"
  rows="auto" columns="auto,auto,*,auto,auto,auto,auto" class="exocortex-header">

  <Label col="0" text="Exocortex" tap="{{ onShowHomeTap }}"
    class="exocortex-header-home" verticalAlignment="center" />

  <Label col="1" text="&#x2014;" class="exocortex-header-sep" verticalAlignment="center" />

  <!-- Whatever is foreground ON THE GLASSES. "Home" when that is the
       Exocortex home screen itself, which is what glassesForegroundLabel
       already reports for the cover glance. -->
  <Label col="2" text="{{ glassesForegroundLabel }}"
    class="exocortex-header-app" verticalAlignment="center" />

  <Label col="3" text="&#x2014;" class="exocortex-header-sep" verticalAlignment="center" />

  <Label col="4" text="{{ connectionStatusLabel }}" tap="{{ onConnectionStatusTap }}"
    class="exocortex-header-status" verticalAlignment="center" />

  <Label col="5" text="&#x26A0;&#xFE0F;" tap="{{ onWarningIconTap }}"
    visibility="{{ warningIconVisibility }}"
    class="exocortex-header-warning" verticalAlignment="center" />

  <Label col="6" text="&#x2699;" tap="{{ onSettingsHubTap }}"
    class="exocortex-header-settings" verticalAlignment="center" />

</GridLayout>
